course: dictionary
lesson: 6767
title: Fact or opinion
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An opinion is what you think or believe about something. It may not be the same as what others think. «Paris is the best city» is an opinion, because someone could easily think another city is best. An opinion can also be advice or a judgement from an expert, like a doctor's opinion.
explain: A fact can be checked and proved true or false. «Paris is in France» can be checked on a map. Ask yourself: can I check this? If yes, it is a fact. If it is what someone thinks, it is an opinion.
explain: Alice snaps «Nobody asked your opinion», and then the Hatter asks «Who's making personal remarks now?» Alice has done the very thing she scolded him for. Everyone has opinions, so listen politely and disagree kindly.
fact: An opinion is what you think or believe about something.
fact: A fact can be proved true or false, like «Paris is in France».
fact: An opinion poll asks around one or two thousand people chosen to match the country; it gives a good guess, not a sure answer.
fact: «Second opinion» means asking another expert, like a doctor, to check what the first one said.
fact: Reports should be facts, things that can be checked, not opinions.
exercise: «Paris is the best city in the world.» Is this a fact or an opinion? | *An opinion, because someone could think another city is best | A fact, because Paris is a city | A fact, because it can be checked
exercise: «Paris is in France.» Is this a fact or an opinion? | An opinion, because France is a big country | *A fact, because it can be checked on a map | An opinion, because it is what someone thinks
exercise: Which sentence is an opinion? | Chocolate is the tastiest sweet | Chocolate is sold in shops | *Chocolate is made from cocoa beans, and you can check that | Chocolate bars have wrappers
test: Dad says, «In my opinion, the film was too long.» What is his opinion? | That films are made in Hollywood | *That the film was too long | That the film has ninety minutes
test: Which sentence is a fact that can be checked? | *The River Thames flows through London | Mango is the best fruit | Football is more fun than swimming
exam: Why does an opinion poll give a good guess, not a sure answer? | It asks only a few people | *It asks around one or two thousand people, not everyone, so it is a good guess | It asks only children | It is always wrong
